# Teardown and lifecycle

- Every long-lived subscribe needs an end: `unsubscribe`, `take`, `takeUntil`, or framework helpers.
- Web components / Lit: `takeUntil(destroy$)` in `disconnectedCallback` / controller `hostDisconnected`.
- Angular: prefer `async` pipe, `toSignal`, or `takeUntilDestroyed()`.
- Fetch wrappers: abort with `AbortController` in Observable teardown; ignore `AbortError` as stream error.
- Unsubscribe is idempotent; still design producers with safe teardown.

```js
// ✅ WC / Lit style
const destroy$ = new Subject();
source$.pipe(takeUntil(destroy$)).subscribe(/* ... */);
// on disconnect:
destroy$.next();
destroy$.complete();
```
